rew up with a father who came here as an immigrant and pushed a push cart when he was seven years old. He worked on a laundry wagon when there was still a horse on a laundry wagon in New York City. At 13, he fell off the laundry wagon. The horse broke and ran away and pulled him off the laundry cart and he fell into a spike that went through his leg. Go ahead, laugh if you want. That's the way how sick those are. So I come from very hard-working people, from immigrant people, and I see the world through the eyes of those people. Now, I've been highly educated with two masters degrees and a PhD. Trust me, I have a highly educated view of the world. I'm a scientist by training. Don't try to take it away from me because I won't permit it. You can't do it to me. I have a scientist training, and I'm looking at the political world for the eyes of an objective scientist, and I'm telling you how I see it. You don't have to agree with me, but try to refute it. Try to refute the fact that here's a mass rapist than genocidal maniac, Al-Baghdadi, who is killed under Trump's watch, and the vermin in the media, and the filth in a Democrat party, try to take that away from him, denying the world knowledge of this Hitlerite guy. denying the world knowledge of what was just done. And all the while that I'm doing this, the state is burning. The state is burning and Pelosi is nowhere to be found. The state is burning and Feinstein's probably figuring out how she can finagle a little money out of it somehow. I'm sure Feinstein's trying to get a contract or two out of someone to see if she can make a little gelt off it. Pelosi too, I mean, they're in the big business people. I'm sure they'll make, through three, four, five front companies, they'll make fortunes off the fire. Especially since the governor's part of the whole Getty machine. Where do you think he came from? The Getty machine. What are you talking about? You know, you talk about the Tammany Hall in New York. San Francisco and California looks like Getty Hall to me. So tonight live somewhere in a hidden location is about 98 people. It only seats less, but they jam their in savage-nation-live.com. The event is on. The event is on. And if you can't be there, no one could be there now. You want to download the event and see the entire party, you see the crowd, and you'll see my performance, see how well I did. You can download it for like $9.95, less than a beer in a local hotel, and you judge for yourself what you think tonight. I got to get from here to there today in one piece. I got to get today this morning in traffic. from a county where there's no lights, no electricity to San Francisco, so I can do this show. And I'm doing this show from San Francisco. Beautiful city when you look down upon it from the studio down onto the streets. It's a sunny day. The air is clear today. Yesterday looked like nuclear winter. It's a nice place to walk around. And by the way, there's something interesting going on in San Francisco. The streets are cleaner. There are fewer bums in the streets. The businessmen are sweeping in front of their stores and restaurants. Even in Chinatown, which is usually filthy, it looks like a slum in Hong Kong. Even in Chinatown, the Chinese restaurants and such vegetable markets are stacking their used cardboard neatly. I don't understand what's going on. It looks to me like the mothers and fathers who run this city. have either put out new laws or something's going on even see street sweepers now something's weird going on the city's looking cleaner maybe someone could tell me what's happening I don't see as many filthy degenerate bums running around the are here and there but not that many and uh... the streets are cleaner there must be a new ordinance that i don't know about businesses are sweeping cleaning washing maybe they put out some laws finally i hope so it's a beautiful city and i love this city came here and i became very very much at home i don't like it 